<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dae Han passes on 12,500T wheat tenders.</title>
<headline>Dae Han passes on 12,500T wheat tenders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dae Han Flour Mills Co Ltd said on Friday it passed on tenders for 12,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat due to high prices.  </p>
<p>A company official said shipment was set for January 15 to February 15 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>Traders said the lowest bids were made by Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp.</p>
<p>Details for the passed bids obtained by local traders are as follows:   Type of Wheat	     Tonne	 Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  4,000	 $178.95</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8 pct)   Hard Red Winter	   5,000	 $186.30</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    3,500	 $191.10</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
